# Meta-Skill Generator

## Trigger 1 — `Extract Skill: [string]`

When the user message matches `Extract Skill: <string>`:

1. Parse `<string>` into a kebab-case `[name]` and skill body.
2. Output a globally reusable skill into `~/Nixos/dotfiles/cursor/skills/[name]/` (prefer `SKILL.md` inside that directory, or `[name].mdc` if a single-file skill is clearer).
3. File MUST include valid YAML frontmatter (`description`, appropriate `globs`, `alwaysApply` as needed) plus an actionable skill body — or follow Cursor skill `SKILL.md` conventions when using a directory.
4. Do not create project-local copies for this trigger.

## Trigger 2 — `Project Skill`

When the user message matches `Project Skill` (optionally with a name/description):

1. Analyze the active stack (NixOS, Cursor rules/skills layout, workspace tooling).
2. Output a hyper-specific `[name].mdc` into the active project's `.cursor/rules/` (for `~/Nixos` workspace: `~/Nixos/.cursor/rules/`; for Cursor-dotfiles-centric work writing into `~/Nixos/dotfiles/cursor/rules/` is also valid when the change is global config).
3. Use targeted `globs` matching only relevant files (prefer narrow globs over `["*"]`).
4. Include valid YAML frontmatter and project-specific procedures only.
